{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1055281-bill-paxton","id":1055281,"title":"Bill Paxton","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-26T09:33:58-08:00","id":1055281,"title":"Bill Paxton","content":"So, actor (and director and producer) Bill Paxton has died. So, I thought I'd take a moment to mention his work's influence on the World of Darkness. While he only has a small part in the original <b>Terminator</b> film, it eventually lead to his larger part as Pvt. Hudson in <b>Aliens</b>. Both of these had an influence on Mage, particularly on the Technocracy, with the latter being a huge influence on Iteration X and the former influencing facets of the Void Engineers. Then there was <b>Weird Science</b>, which gave the Sons of Ether their default theme song. More seriously, he was part of the nomadic vampire gang in <b>Near Dark</b>, which helped influence Vampire's Sabbat. And finally, <b>Frailty</b>, which for many people was <i>the</i> Hunter: The Reckoning movie. <br /> <br /> If you've never seen any of these films, they are all well worth seeing. As are his more historically oriented work in Tombstone, Apollo 13, and Hatfields &amp; McCoys","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"